    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0263" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/206: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-15T14:00:00-04:00">July 15, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5535. Eacom 26, in reply to your Comea 64 of June 20.<anchor n="99"
                        xml:id="d131-f1"/> Joint Chiefs of Staff have now expressed their views on
                    participation of other Allied forces in occupation zones of Germany.</p>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff consider that from a military point of view the
                    provision of token United States forces in enemy areas controlled <pb
                        facs="0264" n="250" xml:id="pg250"/> by other Allied Nations is inadvisable.
                    However, the Joint Chiefs of Staff consider that there is no objection from a
                    military point of view to the presence in occupied zones of troops of other
                    Allied Nations actually participating in military operations under the authority
                    of the Supreme Commander of the Allied Expeditionary Force.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d131-f1" n="99" xml:id="d131-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 4900, Comea 64, June 20, 7 p.m., from London, asked for additional views
                    on the question of stationing token forces within occupied Germany (740.00119
                    EAC/206).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
